@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch1215corr-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Fresh narrow lineage: SEN0414 Chapters 12 to 15 corrections"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch1215corr_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment "1.7.0 (2026-11-26): Backlog stage of Lineage12: the register root, the backlog, 20 stories with acceptance criteria and links to the objectives they move and the deliverables they satisfy, and the lineage's own Definition of Done. Tasks follow in the planning stage, where each is produced by a planning event.",
        "1.8.0 (2026-11-26): Planning stage of Lineage12: four packages (one per chapter, the last also carrying the closing stories), four time-boxed iterations that match them, and the planning of the first iteration only (refinement, planning events, 14 typed tasks). Iterations 2 to 4 are planned when they start, by small steps. Dates are forecasts, never deadlines.",
        """1.0.0 (2026-11-26): Mission stage only (one stage per version). Opened on the owner's choice of 2026-11-26 08:37 Istanbul ('Chapters 12-15, as they are the lecture subjects incoming in the next weeks') after the read-only sweep of all chapters.
ORDINAL AND ONE-AT-A-TIME CHECK: the live register files were read on 2026-11-26. Lineage10 (chapters 16 and 17) is LS_Achieved and archived (register 1.52.0, with a correction note in 1.53.0); Lineage11 (chapters 10 and 11) is LS_Archived (1.59.0). No other lineage of this repository is open, so only this lineage runs. The highest ordinal in the register and its archives is 11; the next free ordinal is 12.
VERIFIED GAPS (live files measured 2026-11-26 with the deck checks run by /tmp/w/deckchecks.sh (deck standard 1.3.0, fit, layout, notes, overlap, reader notes, story prose) and cme_material_check 1.0.2 on the newest deck and page of each chapter; logs of the measurement kept in 08-tooling/lineage12-opening/). Chapter 12 (deck 2.0.0, page 9.97.0): 42 of 48 notes outside 60 to 140 words; 2 of 38 titles under 4 words; 1 content slide without one thing to look at; 96 of 96 code checks with a prompt marker; 53 of 53 code frames do not parse; 59 lambda occurrences in the page (2 of 53 frames); 3 of 53 frames not found in the page; 9 analogy slides; 52 notes with presenter directions or think-of statements; 28 story-prose findings; fit check refuses slide 16 (two frames overlap); layout check 1 item. Chapter 13 (deck 2.0.0, page 9.96.0): 45 of 51 notes outside 60 to 140 words; 1 of 41 titles under 4 words; 1 content slide without one thing to look at; 102 of 102 prompt markers; 56 of 56 code frames do not parse; 74 lambda occurrences in the page (1 of 56 frames); 10 analogy slides; 53 reader-note findings; 42 story-prose findings. Chapter 14 (deck 2.0.0, page 9.98.0): 45 of 51 notes outside the range; 4 of 42 titles under 4 words; 1 content slide without one thing to look at; 101 of 101 prompt markers; 55 of 55 code frames do not parse; 191 lambda occurrences in the page; 10 analogy slides; 51 reader-note findings; 42 story-prose findings. Chapter 15 (deck 2.0.0, page 9.97.0): 51 of 53 notes outside the range; 1 of 44 titles under 4 words; 1 content slide without one thing to look at; 105 of 105 prompt markers; 57 of 57 code frames do not parse; 228 lambda occurrences in the page; 12 analogy slides; 49 reader-note findings; 35 story-prose findings; fit check refuses slide 34. Deck standard 1.3.0 fails D7 and D10 on all four decks. The story-repeat check lists no repeat by link for chapters 12 to 15; chapter 12 shares the name Ken Thompson with chapters 8, 9 and 10, listed for a person to read.
NOT MEASURED YET (named, not dropped): whether the pages carry analogy text in their visible content; whether each page has the menu item that runs the slide examples in order; whether the chapter code, the page and the lab libraries carry matching code. They are measured in the scope stage before any goal rests on them.
WHY A NEW LINEAGE: Lineage10 and Lineage11 are closed; a closed lineage is revived only in extraordinary cases. Chapters 12 to 15 are a different closeable slice, chosen by the owner because they are the next lecture subjects.
REDUCING REWORK: each deck is rebuilt once through the generic chapter builder from a spec and each page through the lambda-free A-box maker and the page test that chapters 16 and 17 passed; the conversion pattern of Lineage10 is reused, not rebuilt. Chapters 1 to 9 and 18 to 20 follow in later narrow lineages."""@en,
        "1.1.0 (2026-11-26): Scope stage only (one stage per version): the scope statement with its areas, deliverables and exclusions, derived from the Mission stage's verified gaps (Lineage Operating Discipline v163.0.7, 3d: the chain is derived from the scope taxonomy). Each area is answered by a goal in the goal stage, each exclusion by a goal that guards it. The three gaps named NOT MEASURED in 1.0.0 are scope items here and are measured, by reading the page's own menu and code, before any goal rests on them."@en,
        "1.10.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 1 (chapter 12) done. States moved in place in this merged file (1.9.0 removed from the working tree, kept in git history): the six stories and fourteen tasks of the iteration are Done, each with an audit note naming its evidence. Release record: 07-lineage/reports/REPORT_Lineage12_ch12_release_and_review_v1_0_0.md."@en,
        "1.11.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 2 (chapter 13) done. The four chapter 13 stories were groomed into nine tasks in this version, after the work had been done (a deviation: the tasks should have reached the register first); stories and tasks are Done, each task with an audit note naming its evidence. Release record: 07-lineage/reports/REPORT_Lineage12_ch13_release_and_review_v1_0_0.md."@en,
        "1.12.0 (2026-11-26): the four chapter 14 stories are groomed into nine typed tasks (Proposed) BEFORE any chapter 14 file is changed, as the lessons require; the stories stay Proposed. Iteration 2 had its tasks written after the work; this is the correction for iteration 3."@en,
        "1.13.0 (2026-11-26): Chapter 14 spec stage done: the three spec tasks and ST12_Spec_14 are Done, each task with an audit note naming its evidence (tasks were groomed first in 1.12.0)."@en,
        "1.14.0 (2026-11-26): Chapter 14 deck stage done: deck 3.0.0 (51 slides, 24 examples, 6 stories) and ST12_Deck_14 are Done."@en,
        "1.15.0 (2026-11-26): Chapter 14 page stage done: page 9.103.0 and ST12_Page_14 are Done."@en,
        "1.16.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 3 (chapter 14) done: deck 3.1.0, page 9.104.0 and the release record; ST12_Release_14 and its two tasks are Done. Chapter 14 tasks reached the register before the work, as the lessons require. Note: the commit ead38e3 was pushed without the register by a command slip (the register file was removed before its new version was written); this version restores it."@en,
        "1.2.0 (2026-11-26): Revision of the scope stage (a stage may be revised by a stage revision, Lineage Operating Discipline v163.0.7, 3f). Cause: running `backlog_next_act check --all` (framework SHACL 1.229.0, read from the clone updated the same day) on 1.0.0 and 1.1.0 lists rules the stage did not answer: every area needs a location and a counted measure (ScopeAreaShape), every area, deliverable and exclusion a layer (ScopeLayerShape), every deliverable a quoted mission clause (DeliverableProvenanceShape), every exclusion a named concern (ScopeExclusionShape), the scope a list of required deliverables (ScopeContentShape), the mission a decider and a stated outcome (MissionShape, MissionOutcomeShape). Added here: those statements. No mission amendment is made (see the audit note of Scope12). The two rules that wait for later stages (a goal advancing the mission, a goal of each facing, an objective measuring each area) are answered by the goal and objective stages. Measured facts for the area counts are those of 1.0.0 (logs in 08-tooling/lineage12-opening/)."@en,
        "1.3.0 (2026-11-26): Goal stage only (one stage per version). Derived from Scope12, not from a list of gaps (Lineage Operating Discipline v163.0.7, 3d): one mission-facing goal; scope-facing goals that between them cover all eight areas; one containment-facing goal; one exclusion-facing goal for each of the five exclusions. Each goal states the benefit of what the work implements; the conditions of the record are measured by the objectives of the next stage. The Owner's reading of the re-cut notes and balloons is a quality of this development, named in the mission-facing goal, not a condition recorded elsewhere."@en,
        "1.4.0 (2026-11-26): Objective stage only (one stage per version). Each goal is measured by objectives (22 in all), each metric derived from its goal, each with a counted, derived or judged measurement and a query that reads it, a baseline measured on 2026-11-26 (logs in 08-tooling/lineage12-opening/; the balloon, own-version and example counts from the files named in each query) and a baseline observation. The six goals that are met by absence (containment and five exclusions) carry the direction Hold: their figure is read from git or by the reviewers at every observation and can rise. Checkpoint dates are forecasts from backlog_date_plan, never deadlines. Forecast dates: see each objective's rationale. The goals of 1.3.0 are given their origin (session drafted) and their accountable decider (the Owner) here, as the stage rules now require."@en,
        "1.5.0 (2026-11-26): The Owner's ruling on the menu item is recorded and the mission widened (G216). Question put 2026-11-26 (answer options 1 to 3); answer 09:29 Istanbul: '1, yes. It should be a common rule for all chapters.' The ruling is a GovernanceRuling enforced by a shape in 03-materials/sen0414_page_shapes_v1_0_0.ttl (tested on the five newest page A-boxes of chapters 12 to 16: each fails as shipped and passes with the menu item planted; log 08-tooling/lineage12-opening/page_runorder_shape_test_v1_0_0.log). One objective is added for it, measured by that shape. The rule is common to all chapters; this lineage applies it to chapters 12 to 15 only, and the shape already shows chapter 16 without it, so the other chapters are named gaps for their own lineages (chapters 1 to 11 and 16 to 20 are excluded here by Excl12_OtherChapters)."@en,
        "1.6.0 (2026-11-26): Correction of the forecast dates (append, never edit): checkpoint and forecast dates move from 2026-12-07 and 12-08 to 2026-11-28 and 11-29, with the basis read from git. The older dates stay visible in 1.4.0 and 1.5.0."@en,
        "1.9.0 (2026-11-26): Merged register. Deltas 1.0.0 to 1.8.0 combined into one file; hasState, hasLineageStatus, hasMissionOutcome, checkpointDate, hasForecastDate and hasForecastRationale take their latest value (the corrected dates of 1.6.0 stand; the earlier dates stay in git history); every other statement is kept. Moves recorded here: the lineage is In progress, story ST12_Template_RunOrder and its first task are InProgress (iteration 1 starts)."@en ;
    owl:priorVersion <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1215corr-lineage/1.15.0> ;
    owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1215corr-lineage/1.16.0> ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.16.0" .

ex:Blueprint12 a backlog:Blueprint ;
    rdfs:label "What the chapters 12 to 15 corrections are about"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage12 ;
    backlog:blueprintFor ex:Backlog12 ;
    backlog:hasDomainEntity ex:DE12_Deck,
        ex:DE12_Page,
        ex:DE12_Review,
        ex:DE12_Spec .

ex:Blueprint12Root a backlog:Blueprint ;
    rdfs:label "What the chapters 12 to 15 corrections are about (register root)"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage12 ;
    backlog:blueprintFor ex:Register_Ch1215corr ;
    backlog:hasDomainEntity ex:DE12_Deck,
        ex:DE12_Page,
        ex:DE12_Review,
        ex:DE12_Spec .

ex:MissionAmendment12_1 a backlog:MissionAmendment ;
    rdfs:label "Mission 12 adds the menu item that runs the slide examples in order"@en ;
    backlog:amendedBy backlog:Owner ;
    backlog:amendedMissionStatement "The chapter 12 (Command-Line Programs), chapter 13 (Web Scraping), chapter 14 (Excel Spreadsheets) and chapter 15 (Google Sheets) decks and interactive pages, already released, are corrected so that they meet the owner's rulings on decks and pages (one thing taught per slide, notes that carry the lecture and speak to the reader, a Slide code tab, plain code without prompts, only taught Python, no everyday analogies, checks and reviews recorded before release), with each chapter's approved content, stories and examples unchanged except where a ruling forces a change, reusing the conversion built for chapters 10, 11, 16 and 17. Every chapter page also carries a top menu item that runs the chapter's slide examples in order, a rule for every chapter of the course." ;
    backlog:amendmentReason "The mission of 1.0.0 did not name the menu item; the scope must not require what the mission does not say, so the mission is widened, never the scope stretched." ;
    backlog:amendmentRuling ex:Ruling12_RunInOrder ;
    backlog:amendsMission ex:Mission12 .

